  "date-post-text": "05 December 2024",
  "rt-blog-html": "\n          <h2>Do you know <a href=\"https://www.foodles.co/\"><strong>Foodles</strong></a> ? </h2>\n          <p>It is THE innovative solution of connected fridges coupled with a daily order service and customized catering modules. </p>\n          <p><a href=\"https://www.foodles.co/\"><strong>Foodles</strong></a> offers a new model of canteen in companies, in communities... fresh, varied and especially \"<em> on demand</em> \" throughout the day, the approach is very attractive. We talk about it in detail in this episode!</p>\n          <blockquote><strong><em><br>\"Many companies have realized that the restaurant business of tomorrow can no longer be like yesterday: different consumer expectations, a need for wider hours for the restaurant space, the need to rely on restaurants to create a unique experience.\"</em></strong></blockquote>\n          <p><br><strong>Amaury Lefébure - VP Sales at Foodles</strong> - is the guest speaker in this new episode on <a href=\"/en/blog/collective-catering-losses-waste-management\"><strong>foodservice</strong></a> new generation of foodservices.</p>\n          <p>Partial reopening of corporate offices, new consumer habits, experience on catering spaces, innovation on the market .... an enriching exchange to be listened to urgently!<br><br>Good listening!</p>\n          <figure style=\"padding-bottom:33.75%\" class=\"w-richtext-align-center w-richtext-figure-type-video\">\n            <div>\n              <iframe src=\"https://widget.ausha.co/index.html?chanId=brd64SKN4weM&amp;showId=brpMZCZkNxWJ&amp;color=%23333333&amp;display=horizontal&amp;v=2&amp;height=200px&amp;autonext=1&amp;podcastId=oaN2PCNR8gew\" frameborder=\"0\"></iframe>\n            </div>\n          </figure>\n          <h2>Guest of the week</h2>\n          <figure>\n            <div><img loading=\"lazy\" alt src=\"/assets/cdn.prod.website-files.com/63f501f2fcfc599ea419f99b/63f501f3fcfc59aa361a00aa_amaury_lefebure.avif\"></div>\n            <figcaption>Amaury Lefébure, VP Sales at Foodles</figcaption>\n          </figure>\n          <h3><strong>Did you like this episode?</strong></h3>\n          <p><em>Feel free to listen to our other episodes and rate our podcast on your favorite platform.</em></p>\n        ",
  "div-class": null,
